  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "Jesus shall reign where'er the sun",
        "does his successive journeys run;",
        "his kingdom stretch from shore to shore,",
        "till moons shall wax and wane no more."
      ],
      [
        "People and realms of ev'ry tongue",
        "dwell on His love with sweetest song;",
        "and infant voices shall proclaim",
        "their early blessings on His Name."
      ],
      [
        "Let ev'ry creature rise and bring",
        "His holiest off'rings to our King;",
        "angels descend with songs again,",
        "and earth repeat the loud amen."
      ],
      [
        "Praise God, from whom all blessings flow;",
        "praise Him, all creatures here below;",
        "praise Him above, ye heav'nly host,",
        "praise Father, Son, and Holy Ghost."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "2/2 time written in quarter-note beats. Verse 1, soprano (melody) line, verified against the Mutopia LilyPond score. Slurred notes carry one syllable over two or more notes. No simplification needed. Range 1 to high 1. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–4: Isaac Watts (1719) as printed in A Selection of Hymns, Used in the Parish Church … Ulverston (1863), Hymn 60, which closes with Thomas Ken's doxology (1674); text from Wikisource (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/A_Selection_of_Hymns,_Used_in_the_Parish_Church,_and_the_Church_of_the_Holy_Trinity,_Ulverston/Hymn_60).",
  "verified": true
